# Production build config for the SPA — committed ON PURPOSE.
#
# Vite INLINES VITE_* into the bundle at build time, so whatever lands here is public by
# definition; Clerk publishable keys are meant to be shipped to the browser (a pk is just
# `pk_live_`/`pk_test_` + base64 of the Frontend API host). NEVER put a real secret in this
# file: it is not git-ignored, and anything here ends up in dist/assets/*.js.
#
# The instance must match the backend's CLERK_DOMAIN / CLERK_JWKS_URL (PLAN §3b) — the SPA
# authenticates against the instance whose JWKS the backend trusts. Ours is the Clerk
# production instance at https://clerk.seekeru.tech (pk derived from that host, not pasted
# from a dashboard).
#
# AI HERE: build-time inlining makes this image environment-specific. Acceptable while prod
# is the only deployed env; when staging arrives (different pk) switch to runtime injection
# or a second build — see PLAN D14.
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_Y2xlcmsuc2Vla2VydS50ZWNoJA==
